# Financial-ledger client walkthrough (smalt emulator)

Browser console → smaltFetch → Cosmos ETag-CAS entry commit →
Service Bus settlement queues → Event Hubs audit telemetry.

## 0. Endpoints (smalt)

| Face | Endpoint | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Cosmos REST (data plane) | `https://localhost:8443` | `lib/smalt/egress/CosmosRoutes.ex:18` (`POST /app/transactions`), `:61-205` |
| ETag CAS | `If-Match` on document writes | `lib/smalt/data_plane/cosmos.ex:133` |
| Service Bus (settlement queues) | AMQP `localhost:5672` | `lib/smalt/messaging/amqp` |
| Event Hubs (audit telemetry) | AMQP `localhost:5673` | `lib/smalt/messaging/event_hubs/listener.ex:3` |
| MCP tool surface | `https://localhost:9545` | `lib/smalt/mcp/` |

## 1. Browser console — commit one balanced entry (Cosmos ETag-CAS)

Paste in the browser console of the Sovereign Console (networking only
through `lib/smalt.ts` `smaltFetch` — raw `fetch` is ESLint-banned):

```js
// The account document holds the running balance; its _etag is the CAS token.
const acct = await smaltFetch("/app/dbs/ledgerdb/colls/accounts/docs/acct-1001");
const debitLeg  = { account: "acct-1001", debitAmount: 250.00, creditAmount: null };
const creditLeg = { account: "acct-2002", debitAmount: null, creditAmount: 250.00 };

const entry = {
  id: "je-2026-0001",                  // fin:entryId — idempotency key (duplicates refuse)
  entryId: "je-2026-0001",
  postedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  casEtag: acct._etag,                 // concurrency law: commit only via If-Match CAS
  postings: [debitLeg, creditLeg],     // sum(debits) must equal sum(credits)
};

// ETag-CAS commit: second writer with a stale _etag gets 412 Precondition Failed.
const res = await smaltFetch("/app/dbs/ledgerdb/colls/entries/docs", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "If-Match": entry.casEtag },
  body: JSON.stringify(entry),
});
console.log(res.status);               // 201 created, or 412 = concurrent writer won
```

An unbalanced entry (debits 250 / credits 240) or a duplicate `entryId`
is refused by the pack gates (gates/010, gates/030) at graph admission —
before any CAS commit is attempted.

## 2. Service Bus — settlement workflow queues

Each settlement stage owns one queue; entries flow stage→stage; SQL
filter rules route by stage index (SB 5672):

```
settle-capture (stage 1) -> settle-enrich (stage 2) -> settle-settle (stage 3) -> settle-audit (stage 4)
```

Stage individuals in the ontology (`fin:Capture`, `fin:Enrich`,
`fin:Settle`, `fin:Audit`) bind `fin:queueName` per stage; forward
leg via MCP 9545 or an AMQP client pointed at loopback 5672.

## 3. Event Hubs — audit telemetry

Every stage transition emits an audit event to `eh-audit-ledger`
(EH 5673); consumer groups replay it for the audit trail:

```
POST /app/transactions            (Cosmos batch commit)
  -> SB settle-capture            (stage 1 enqueued)
  -> SB settle-enrich / settle    (workflow advances)
  -> EH eh-audit-ledger           (per-stage audit telemetry)
```

## 4. Gate contract

| Gate | Refuses when |
|---|---|
| `gates/010_unbalanced_entry.rq` | sum(debit) != sum(credit) on any entry |
| `gates/020_missing_account_ref.rq` | posting w/o account, dangling account, <2 legs |
| `gates/030_duplicate_entry_id.rq` | duplicate fin:entryId across entries |
